    "body": "## Summary\n\nImplements ADR-018: state pseudo-classes for the HoneyBee Browser. Closes #136.\n\n`<a href>` now behaves like a real browser's:\n- **blue** (`#0000EE`) when unvisited\n- **purple** (`#551A8B`) when visited\n- **lighter blue** (`#0055EE`) when hovered\n- **clicking** a link navigates to it\n\nBefore this PR, `<a>` was styled blue by a static `a { color: #0000EE }` rule and clicking did nothing. Every link looked identical regardless of state, and the only way to load a page was typing in the URL bar.\n\n## Commits\n\n| Commit | Scope |\n|---|---|\n| `59d2042` | `RenderState` plumbing (`visited_urls`, `hovered_element`, `pointer_x/y`, `base_url`) threaded through `cascade()` |\n| `c1c4dbc` | Parser recognizes `:link` / `:visited` / `:hover`; matcher uses `RenderState`; specificity counts each as class weight |\n| `92143bf` | UA stylesheet: `a { color }` → `a:link` / `a:visited` / `a:hover` |\n| `1ff7f9e` | `RenderPipeline::record_visit` populates `visited_urls`; relative-href resolution against base URL |\n| `834be39` | `layout::hit_test`; `LineFragment::element`; `Gtk::EventControllerMotion` drives `hovered_element` |\n| `a50e202` | Click-navigation via `Gtk::GestureClick`; `honeybee::resolve_url` public API; **fix: clear `hovered_element` on DOM replacement** (use-after-free segfault) |\n| `aaa334e` | Docs: ADR-018 status → Implemented; README row; ADR index gains 017 + 018 |\n\n## Key design decisions\n\n- **State-tracking model**, not per-element storage. `RenderState` holds `visited_urls` (set of resolved absolute URL strings), `hovered_element` (raw pointer into current DOM), and `base_url` (current page's URL for resolving relative hrefs). No `dom::Element` fields for pseudo-class state.\n- **`honeybee::resolve_url`** in `base/url.{hpp,cpp}` — one canonical implementation used by both the CSS matcher (to decide \"is this `<a>`'s target in `visited_urls`?\") and the browser layer (to fetch on click). Guarantees the string marked visited is byte-identical to the string fetched.\n- **`LineFragment::element`** carries source-element identity through line breaking. Without it, hover over `<a>` inside `<p>` could only return `<p>` (inline elements are flattened during layout). Also enables click-navigation for free.\n- **`hovered_element` is cleared in `render()` before `doc_` is replaced** — the click path segfaulted without this because `hovered_element` outlived its DOM. Fix at the source (only place `doc_` is replaced), not as a defensive check in the matcher.\n\n## Verified behavior\n\nScreenshots confirmed all states (manually, in a running GTK window):\n\n| State | Link color |\n|---|---|\n| No hover, unvisited | `#0000EE` blue |\n| Hover, unvisited | `#0055EE` lighter blue |\n| No hover, visited | `#551A8B` purple |\n| Hover, visited | `#0055EE` lighter blue (hover wins) |\n| After navigating away and back | stays purple |\n\nClick-navigation was tested explicitly for the three crash-point paths that surfaced in review:\n\n1. Click a hovered link → page loads, no crash\n2. Move mouse after load → hover fires against new DOM, no crash\n3. Click a second link (second DOM replacement) → no crash\n\n## Test count\n\n- Before: 228 cases, 881 assertions (main at `cfa9652`)\n- After: **237 cases, 905 assertions**\n- New coverage: `[url][resolve]` (4 cases), `[css][cascade][pseudo]` (+4 cases), `[layout][hit-test]` (3 cases), plus parser + specificity cases in `[css][selectors]`\n- Zero warnings, zero failures\n\n## Not included (deferred to future ADRs)\n\n- Structural pseudo-classes (`:first-child`, `:nth-child`)\n- Logical pseudo-classes (`:not()`, `:is()`)\n- Remaining state (`:focus`, `:active`, `:target`)\n- `:visited` privacy restrictions (real browsers limit `getComputedStyle` on `:visited` to prevent history leaks; out of scope for a local browser)\n- Back/forward navigation buttons (still stubs)\n- `:hover` restyle-only fast path (currently triggers full `relayout()` on hover transitions — v1 correctness over v1 performance)\n\n## ADR\n\n`docs/decisions/018-pseudo-classes.md` — status now **Implemented**.",
